      "side": 1,
      "message": "Question: when *no* entry fits its reported frame and nothing is incomplete (e.g. `ico_oversized_512x384.ico`), we now return `kSuccess` with a codec where every decode returns `kInvalidScale` (before this CL: `kInvalidInput`). What is the reason to prefer this?\n\n- Is this required by `icon-decoding.html`? If yes, could you say in the CL description which icon(s) need this?\n- `kInvalidScale` for a request at exactly `getInfo().dimensions()` is unusual for an `SkCodec`. Callers usually read it as \"try another size\", not \"this image is broken\". `kInvalidInput` from `MakeFromStream` seems like a more accurate signal for \"complete data, nothing decodable\".\n\nIf there is no client that needs metadata from an undecodable ICO, I would prefer to keep returning `kInvalidInput` in this case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 341,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "5e93163b48d2ba121a40f0247c8a0eef63a76f8d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
